The '''2013 UEFA Super Cup''' was the 38th [[UEFA Super Cup]], an annual [[Association football|football]] match organised by UEFA and contested by the reigning champions of the two main European club competitions, the [[UEFA Champions League]] and the [[UEFA Europa League]]. In a repeat of the [[2012 UEFA Champions League Final]], the match featured [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]], the winners of the [[2012–13 UEFA Champions League]], and [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]], the winners of the [[2012–13 UEFA Europa League]]. Having beaten Bayern in the 2012 Champions League Final, it was Chelsea's second consecutive appearance in the Super Cup.<ref>{{cite web|title=2012 UEFA Super Cup|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/history/2012/|date=26 May 2013|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations}}</ref> It was played at the [[Fortuna Arena]] in [[Prague]], Czech Republic, on 30 August 2013, and was the first to be held away from the [[Stade Louis II]] in Monaco since it became a one-legged match in [[1998 UEFA Super Cup|1998]].<ref name="stadium">{{cite web|url=http://www.uefa.org/about-uefa/executive-committee/news/newsid=1644074.html|title=Wembley, Amsterdam ArenA, Prague get 2013 finals|website=UEFA.org|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=16 June 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=UEFA EURO 2020, UEFA Super Cup decisions |url=http://www.uefa.org/about-uefa/executive-committee/news/newsid=1836837.html |website=UEFA.org |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=30 June 2012 |access-date=18 March 2013 }}</ref>

Bayern Munich became the first German team to win the UEFA Super Cup, beating Chelsea on penalties after extra time.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/23902597|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130831072020/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/23902597|url-status=dead|archive-date=31 August 2013|title=2013 Super Cup: As it happened |date=31 August 2013|work=BBC Sport|access-date=13 September 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://espnfc.com/news/story/_/id/1537424/bayern-munich-captain-philipp-lahm-eyes-maiden-super-cup-win |title=Philipp Lahm eyes Super Cup win |date=29 August 2013 |work=ESPN |access-date=30 August 2013 }}</ref> It was also the first time the winner of the Super Cup was determined by a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]].<ref>[https://sports.yahoo.com/blogs/soccer-dirty-tackle/victorious-bayern-munich-players-console-romelu-lukaku-decisive-223659118--sow.html Victorious Bayern Munich players console Romelu Lukaku after decisive penalty in UEFA Super Cup]</ref> Chelsea's defeat made them the first team to lose consecutive Super Cups since [[FC Porto|Porto]] in 2004.

==Venue==
[[File:Praha, Slavia, fotbalový stadion (2).jpg|thumb|304x304px|The [[Eden Arena]].]]
The [[Eden Arena]] was announced as the venue of the 2013 UEFA Super Cup on 16 June 2011.<ref name="stadium"/> It opened in May 2008 on the site of the [[Stadion Eden (1953)|former Stadion Eden]].<ref>{{cite news|first=Ladislav|last=Josef|title=Prague celebrates 2013 Super Cup honour|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0250-0c50f41ca710-696a44dbb39d-1000--prague-celebrates-2013-super-cup-honour/|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations|date=17 June 2011|access-date=23 June 2011}}</ref> It is the home stadium of [[SK Slavia Prague]], who play in the [[Czech First League]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Venue guide: Prague|url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0250-0c50fe2e3a31-8715240c498c-1000--venue-guide-prague/|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations}}</ref>

